references/
# Skill reference files are source, not fetched cache. Untracking them is how a
# patterns.md truncated at 40,000 chars shipped with no history and no diff.
# Scoped to portable skills on purpose; other references/ dirs stay ignored.
!clean-rag/portable/skills/**/references/
!clean-rag/portable/skills/**/references/**
mcp-rag-server/.rag-index/
indexes/
state/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.events.jsonl
.events.jsonl.lock
.runtime/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
node_modules/
witness/
refinery/
mayor/
crew/
/workspace

# Scratch diff dumps. diff_out.txt was committed once, 728 lines of raw
# `git diff` output that nothing reads.
diff_out.txt
*.diff.txt

# Coverage artifacts
.coverage
.coverage.*
.coveragerc
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# Generated/stale visualization files
graph.json
how-it-works.html

# Runtime databases
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# pip cache
pip/

# Dev-only benchmark scripts
mcp-rag-server/benchmarks/

# pytest instrumentation (generated by pytest-cov)
scripts/tests/sitecustomize.py

# MCP server working state, none of it source. The first two land inside
# whatever project the server is pointed at, which is why they need ignoring
# here. The rest default to the user's home directory and are listed only to
# cover a server configured to write beside the code instead.
.serena/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.semgrep/
.semgrep_logs/
.arxiv-mcp-server/
.osv-scanner-cache/

# A real .mcp.json may only ever contain ${VAR} placeholders, never a resolved
# token. Ignored because a pasted literal secret is a one keystroke mistake and
# this file is not needed in the repo: the installer registers servers at user
# scope from the MCP_SERVERS tables instead.
.mcp.json
